 ## Settings groups
 
 - **Sources:** one card per Source with its switch, fields and verified account facts. GitHub also offers receive-all switches for new Issues, pull requests, comments and default-branch CI. Polling and read limits are under Advanced.
-- **Eval:** the Policy version and rules, followed by **On each Source** and the Eval settings. Each Source tab contains its allowed list, membership sync, admission table and bot list. Sync runs at startup and on **Sync now**. The admission table distinguishes receiving scope, sender membership and whether the message addresses the agent. Eval settings select the accept mode, timeout and assessment model.
+- **Eval:** the Policy version and rules, followed by **On each Source** and the Eval settings. Each Source tab contains its allowed list, membership sync, admission table and bot list. Sync runs at startup and on **Sync now**. The admission table distinguishes receiving scope, sender membership and whether the message addresses the agent. Eval settings select the accept mode, timeout and assessment model. The model picker lists every provider and model in the DSH directory, so any advertised route can be chosen without knowing its ids; the three fields stay editable for a route the directory does not list.
 - **Execution:** worker model, concurrency, directory root, prepare command and blocked commands. Clicking an available variable inserts it into the prepare command.
 - **Communication:** the switch that mirrors communication into a Feishu document. While it is on, every message a person sends and every message the agent sends is appended to one document, in order; turning it off stops appending, and turning it on again opens a new document. The page links to the document it appends to and says when a message failed. Advanced sets the Drive folder a new document is created in and the open IDs granted view access; left empty, the document is created in the bot's own space and granted to the senders the Feishu Policy allows. Work inside a Ticket is not appended.
 - **Prompts:** **Edit** changes team sections, built-in parts and skills. **Full prompt** shows the assembled text and compares it with saved text or defaults. **History** lists versions. Edited built-in parts are marked changed and can be reset; templates list their required placeholders.
